id: pm-gh1554
title: "GH-1554: resume bounded activity reads from a stable event window"
description: The October23 report shows activity limit truncation without a cursor or fixed-window recovery under concurrent writers. Reproduce current producer semantics and implement a stable bounded continuation or explicit fixed-window consistency recovery. Include the since-to-from flag recovery papercut.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1554",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:33:56.767Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T18:24:04.979Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T18:24:04.078Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T18:24:04.078Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: A current temporary-tracker regression proves the omitted event set under concurrent writes; Continuation or fixed-window recovery is bounded and stable for timestamp ties; SDK CLI and MCP share the same completeness contract and since misuse points to from.
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "The SDK provides clock-pinned bounded activity continuation with full normalized matching-content refusal, positional tie preservation and aligned CLI/MCP/contracts/completion. Ordered canonical row hashing bounds additional serialization by the largest row; digest activity separately hashes full source events so hidden patch changes invalidate the cursor. SDK guidance explains consistency, resource bounds and package-safe tracking links."
expected_result: "Recover omitted activity rows through bounded SDK/CLI/MCP pages without lost ties or changed-content reuse, while avoiding a complete serialized copy of large matching sets and preserving Node/Bun behavior."
actual_result: "Full canonical suite passes11208tests with3platform skips at70683/70683statements,54364/54364branches,14551/14551functions and66918/66918lines. Full serialized quality:static passes. Linked activity55tests and guidance/contracts76tests pass; real Zsh/Fish probes and public-SDK Node-to-Bun activity/calendar cursors pass. Identical isolated192MiBold-generation384MiBlogical-patch control exhausts old hashing and returns both pages with new hashing. Exact-head hosted CI and retriggered review remain mandatory merge gates."
