comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T07:33:56.767Z","harness:codex","Intake: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1554. Duplicate checks used request-specific live search and a fresh all-status strict corpus of3071 items with no omissions; related delivered lineage is linked and remains closed. The report is recorded without claiming current reproduction. Intake only, open and unclaimed."
  "2026-10-24T12:00:38.149Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: combine GH1554 and GH1562 in one SDK-first delivery. Bootstrap passed; complete strict all-status read covers 3098 items with no omissions and no prior in_progress items. Full live metadata and verified histories confirm these canonical owners are open, while delivered pm-8nev0o, pm-qh3p and pm-kglq remain closed. Plan: bounded query continuation binds the original clock, normalized query and exact matching rows; later events outside the pinned activity window remain excluded, while changed matching content fails closed with fresh-query guidance. Add CLI/MCP parity, timestamp-tie controls and since-to-from recovery."
  "2026-10-24T12:13:47.772Z","harness:codex","Regression evidence: the same new integration suite ran against isolated pre-fix main ef143cc49 with sandboxed PM roots. All four activity projection cases fail because next_cursor is absent; the calendar case fails because completeness/page fields are absent (5 expected failures, 3 unrelated tests skipped). Current implementation passes all 8 new direct-SDK/CLI/MCP/package cases. Typecheck and focused ESLint pass. Complete repository coverage is running. New queries bind workspace, projection/filter semantics, full matching content and the frozen clock; changed matching content refuses rather than silently restarting or skipping tied rows."
  "2026-10-24T12:15:38.115Z","harness:codex","Operational verification: required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero unresolved/critical/high issues in the14-day Sentry window; telemetry4.77 percent error rate versus6 percent policy and zero missing error-code rows. Independent latest50 production command finishes all match their command_start by installation/session/command/started_at, newest finish8seconds old. Physical queue has0ready/0unacked/0total messages. These are bounded current probes, not proof of all historical actions. Private host/query details remain in ignored local evidence."
  "2026-10-24T12:20:31.698Z","harness:codex","Additional bounded observability check: sentry issue list is:unresolved returns a complete empty result; sentry trace list default window also returns no rows. This does not establish recent trace ingestion. Production telemetry freshness and50/50 lifecycle pairing are independently verified; retain trace-ingestion as a distinct observation, without manufacturing a Sentry error to produce data."
  "2026-10-24T12:31:19.657Z","harness:codex","First full run completed:11189 passed and16 failures across11 files, with no coverage certificate because tests failed. Failures reduce to coupled contracts: context forwarded its focus after cursor into the nested calendar call; shell completion omitted after; flag inventory needed exactly one new declared producer flag; projection parity compared independent evaluation clocks; key-order/summary fixtures needed the additive fields. Fixes preserve the shrinking behavior baseline and original411-token help ceiling: activity help is shortened instead of raising the help budget, canonical flag maximum rises only35to36 for the implemented after capability, and existing context continuation tests retain exact recovery. A focused all-failure sweep precedes another full run."
  "2026-10-24T12:35:57.561Z","harness:codex","The coupled regression sweep is repaired:10 of12 affected files passed first, then the remaining release-readiness and packed continuation files pass34/34 tests after exact help/key-order updates and exposing the existing host npm module through NODE_PATH. Both linked PM test commands pass independently (activity53 tests; calendar38). Context focus cursors no longer leak into the nested calendar producer. New public after discovery, SDK/MCP normalization and Bash/Zsh/Fish completion retain existing flags; full source coverage and full static quality are rerunning without relaxed thresholds."
  "2026-10-24T12:54:41.480Z","harness:codex",Full runtime rerun passes all11205 tests with3 intentional skips. Exact coverage finds one uncovered branch in activity unknown-option conflict recovery (54361/54362 branches; all statements/functions/lines are100percent). Add a CLI-level conflicting since/from case proving no unsafe retry is suggested. Hosted static also caught the catalogue/snapshot generation order; rebuild the regenerated error catalogue before refreshing the contracts fixture. Only this owner is reactivated for those actual edits; pm-gh1562 remains closed/released.
  "2026-10-24T15:37:03.740Z","harness:codex","Two final contract-quality repairs: the shared window-pagination module must be catalogued as a cross-cutting source rather than advertised as a nonexistent executable command; its generator fixture now enforces wildcard ownership. The unchanged contracts-summary token ceiling exposed four excess estimated tokens after adding after. A curated three-flag activity bootstrap now prioritizes limit/after/full while the complete flags-only/help surfaces retain compact and every compatibility spelling. No token ceiling is raised and no capability is removed. Rebuild regenerated catalog before snapshot generation to seal correct source discovery."
  "2026-10-24T15:41:51.682Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit full review completed with two actionable points. Correct the Zsh after source escape and strengthen the existing completion conformance to require one quoted option per physical line and exactly one generated continuation backslash. Narrow the dependency inventory wording via pm comments --edit; preserve the original append-only history event, which was accurate before PR1575 existed. Both findings are being handled in their existing inline threads after the revision is pushed."
  "2026-10-24T15:43:41.627Z","harness:codex","Activity first-page cost accounting: new fixed-window/page/cursor metadata increases the measured default packet from656 to736 estimated tokens while retaining all15 rows and every prior summary field. The old fixture ceiling722 therefore no longer describes this intentional API. Regenerate the measurement with the canonical tool and adopt only the activity-default row with zero new headroom (max736), retaining every other ratchet, the4000-token SDK answer ceiling, discovery ceilings and unbounded negative controls. The curated limit/after/full bootstrap keeps the original contracts-summary and agent-task budgets. This explicitly supersedes the earlier attempt to fit all new metadata under the old activity fixture ceiling."
  "2026-10-24T16:00:35.467Z","harness:codex","Final pre-push verification is running on the revised source. The completion fix passes76 focused contract tests plus an actual Zsh argument-capture probe (19 clean arguments, after and limit present). The added unit refusal case directly exercises source error-guidance with conflicting since/from values and a supplied unsafe fallback; its CLI counterpart separately proves transport behavior. No source coverage exclusions or thresholds changed. Full-suite and static reruns will supply final closure evidence before the revision is pushed and all reviewers are requested again."
  "2026-10-24T16:13:56.884Z","harness:codex","Canonical full-suite proof on the revised implementation: 860 test files pass, one platform-only file skipped; 11206 tests pass and3 platform-only tests skip. Exact V8 coverage is70679/70679 statements,54362/54362 branches,14550/14550 functions and66915/66915 lines, with zero uncovered counts and no altered thresholds or exclusions. Full static assurance is still running. Fresh GitHub intake found reports1576 and1577; both now have canonical open/unclaimed PM owners and one corresponding issue-link comment, preserving the selected continuation delivery scope."
  "2026-10-24T16:34:11.179Z","harness:codex","Final source proof including the counts-only calendar rendering delta: all11206tests pass with3platform skips; exact coverage is70679/70679statements,54364/54364branches,14550/14550functions and66915/66915lines. The first revised static gate caught three newly introduced prose-to-edge gaps, not a runtime failure. Existing scope/reliability evidence now has the corresponding associative edges; the graph ceiling is unchanged. The9agent workflows/25steps and post-closure defect-evidence gate pass. Full static is rerunning before the metadata correction is pushed and full review is requested again."
  "2026-10-24T17:03:40.315Z","harness:codex","Full review-summary audit found four touched query helpers without JSDoc: activity filter resolution, activity row projection, calendar execution inputs and context agenda construction. Add concise invariant-focused documentation to all four; the TypeScript AST census verifies their declarations directly. The out-of-scope recommendation is declined because the user explicitly requested live dependency/security, telemetry/release and GitHub intake documentation in the same delivery. Required hosted checks on the preceding runtime head are all green. CodeRabbit reports the next free included review becomes available about17:25UTC; preserve free-only operation and request the next full review after that window rather than sending duplicate rate-limited comments."
  "2026-10-24T17:05:05.717Z","harness:codex","The four missing helper docstrings are now present with concrete clock, matching-content and cursor-isolation invariants. A TypeScript AST check verifies all four declarations; build, repository docstring quality and focused ESLint pass. Runtime code is unchanged from c544f06cf355e90d0e9781e5265582e462b2167e, whose required hosted checks and exact100percent source coverage are green. Final fresh free CodeRabbit review is scheduled after its explicit quota reset at17:25:07UTC; no paid review or duplicate trigger is used."
  "2026-10-24T17:35:44.222Z","harness:codex","The free full review completed on826010050 with one major scalability finding: createQueryFingerprint currently materializes a canonical serialization of every matching row for each bounded page, including full activity patch payloads and a second digest-source copy. Investigate an incremental canonical content digest using existing hashing primitives, preserve full-content drift refusal and timestamp-tie behavior, and add a direct independent memory/allocation control. Existing generated contracts and runtime gates are green; only this canonical owner is active for the new implementation."
  "2026-10-24T17:49:22.203Z","harness:codex","Incremental fingerprint implementation is verified by the identical isolated child-process fixture against old826010050 and current code: with192MiBV8old-generation limit and384MiBlogical patch content, old hashing aborts with heap exhaustion, while current hashing returns page indices0and1, total1536, remaining1534. The control disables core files for its disposable child; the regression itself is isolated from the test runner. Source tests also prove canonical key-order equivalence, row ordering, unambiguous scalar boundaries and hidden patch mutation refusal across all four activity modes. The10-test continuation suite, build, typecheck and focused ESLint pass; linked tests plus full canonical coverage/static are running. Queries retain their existing full matching-row scan; additional fingerprint serialization is bounded by the largest row. SDK docs state this resource boundary."
  "2026-10-24T18:12:27.642Z","harness:codex","Full incremental-hash verification passes11208tests with3platform skips across860passingfiles. Exact coverage:70683/70683statements,54364/54364branches,14551/14551functions,66918/66918lines. The parallel static attempt exhausted its20-minute build-lease wait while coverage legitimately held the lease; no lock override was used. It is rerunning alone after coverage exited. The public SDK Node-to-Bun probe resumes both activity/calendar cursors with preserved clocks. SDK resource documentation also uses canonical repository URLs for tracker records and explicitly states their npm exclusion."
  "2026-10-24T18:24:03.302Z","harness:codex","Serialized full pnpm quality:static completes successfully on the incremental-hash source and corrected SDK package links. It includes dependency/runtime locks, documentation, exports/lint/duplicates, contracts, package/SDK parity, grammar/flag/refusal/token checks, graph and record integrity, and the governed mutation suite. All local gates for this performance revision are now green. The independent memory before/after control and Node-to-Bun public-SDK continuation proof are retained; no cursor checks, limits, test denominators or assurance thresholds were weakened."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T12:14:30.188Z","harness:codex",A bounded continuation needs both a stable evaluation clock and an identity for the complete matching content. Freezing only timestamps does not protect against backdated writes; an exact matching-set fingerprint must refuse stale pages. Preserve duplicate events using positional identity within the unchanged set.
  "2026-10-24T17:45:32.753Z","harness:codex",Hash canonical matching rows incrementally and keep digest-source events as a fixed-size content digest. Strong stale-content refusal still requires a matching-row scan on every page; avoid an additional complete serialized copy and document the largest-row allocation bound.
